It seems that a navigation node of type "{{TYPE_CONTAINER}}" can no longer have any children, and the action of the first (I believe) child is used instead.

You can see an example of this in the Forum with the "Subscription mode" container.

Replication
# Create a new forum
# View the forum
## *Observe: "{{Subscription mode}}" is a link which does not expand to give options*
# Click the "Subscription mode" navigation link
## *Observe: the mode is toggled between Optional and Automatic"
## *Observe: there is no way to set the mode to "Forced" or "Disabled" from the More menu*


Alternatively, add some code like this to the bottom of {{mod/forum/lib.php::forum_extend_settings_navigation()}}
{code}
    $nodes = [];
    $nodes[] = \navigation_node::create('Example.com', 'https://example.com', \navigation_node::TYPE_SETTING, null, 'COM');
    $nodes[] = \navigation_node::create('Example.org', 'https://example.org', \navigation_node::TYPE_SETTING, null, 'ORG');

    $addto = $forumnode->add(
        'Some new parent container',
        null,
        \navigation_node::TYPE_CONTAINER
    );

    foreach ($nodes as $node) {
        $addto->add_node($node);
    }
{code}
Observe how the "SOme new parent container" is not a container but is now a link for the first child item.
